# Only definitions absent from the pinned MINTEQ database.
# Struvite: Ronteltap, Maurer & Gujer (2007), Water Research 41, 977-984.
# DOI 10.1016/j.watres.2006.11.046; standard pKsp 13.26 at 25 C.
# Kieserite: USGS PHREEQC 3.8.6 pitzer.dat, log K -0.123 at 25 C.
# Both reactions use unit solid activity. H2O activity remains explicit.
PHASES
Sylvite
 KCl = K+ + Cl-
 log_k 0.9
Struvite
 MgNH4PO4:6H2O = Mg+2 + NH4+ + PO4-3 + 6 H2O
 log_k -13.26
Kieserite
 MgSO4:H2O = Mg+2 + SO4-2 + H2O
 log_k -0.123
# Urea is an unhydrolysed neutral product inventory. Identity reaction only:
# no urease kinetics, ammonium conversion or acid/base constant is invented.
SOLUTION_MASTER_SPECIES
 Ure Ure 0 CO(NH2)2 60.0553
SOLUTION_SPECIES
Ure = Ure
 log_k 0
